 "sentences": [
  "Firstly, always add the '@trace_class' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your classes.",
  "Also, always include try statements in your functions.",
  "This helps with error handling and will make your code more robust.",
  "No, just the standard try-except format will do.",
  "But it is important that you incorporate it consistently.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "We'll schedule regular check-ins to ensure you're on track and provide any necessary support.",
  "It's important for the consistency and readability of our code.",
  "From now on, I want you to use annotations for functions.",
  "Annotations provide clarity and help other engineers understand the purpose and usage of your functions.",
  "Always include them, even if the function seems straightforward to you.",
  "Remember, clear and concise annotations are key.",
  "The goal is to provide enough information for someone else to understand the function's input and output without having to dive into the implementation details.",
  "Absolutely.",
  "We want our code to be as accessible and understandable as possible for our colleagues.",
  "It promotes collaboration and makes debugging and maintenance easier down the line.",
  "Also, going forward, I want you to make sure you end all your method names with '_b'.",
  "It's a small detail, but it helps with consistency and makes your code more identifiable."
 ],
